{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/88930-deceived-in-my-chronicle","id":88930,"title":"Deceived in my chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-11T10:54:43-07:00","id":88930,"title":"Deceived in my chronicle","content":"Hi,<br /> I'm about to start M:tC chronicle and I was thonking about main antagonists. I designed one interesting Shuankhsen and I was thinking about someone superior to him, someone like Deceived.<br /> Unfortunately in corebook there is only a little information about them.<br /> <br /> Have you ever tried to put some Lost Guild character into your chronicle? I'm curious about some ideas...<br /> <br /> Also - don't you know whether there will be some sourcebook about antagonists in M:tC?<br /> <br /> thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2492-wenoush","name":"wenoush","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T14:11:23-07:00","id":89034,"title":"","content":"We know VERY LITTLE about the deceived. We basically know three things about them.<br /> 1. They maybe know the secrets of the True Name and Name Magic, which is why they're being pursued by the Scribes.<br /> 2. They probably have much more information about what actually happened in Irem than any other mummy. They probably also have their full memories like the Shuankhsen.<br /> 3. They might have some connection to the mythical state Apotheosis.<br /> They were wiped out because of these things and now they're basically a myth to the arisen.<br /> There will be a book specifically about them called &quot;Book of the Deceived&quot; which is coming out...TBD. They lost a writer recently so who knows how long it will take. Sorry but that's all I know about them. I admire you for actually using them in your game. Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T14:26:03-07:00","id":89045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wenoush</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/88930-deceived-in-my-chronicle#post88930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever tried to put some Lost Guild character into your chronicle? I'm curious about some ideas...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few story hooks I've posted over at the story hooks thread that I've used in actual play.<br /> <br /> .) The Descents of a number of Arisen have recently been ended prematurely. Evidence suggests involvement of the Lost Guild, the Deceived, masters of the occult art of Nomenclature.<br /> <br /> None of the attacked Arisen have thus far been able to successfully defend themselves against the Deceived threat.<br /> <br /> The guilds' hope rests on one of the PCs, who, in her first life in the Nameless Empire, has been an active member of the Lost Guild, until she later decided to quit in order to join one of the other guilds. It is up to her to rebuild her memory of her first life and figure out some defense against the magics of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .) One of the arch-enemies of the meret, a known Deceived member of the Lost Guild, a very dangerous master of nomenclature, shows up. He's obviously having trouble remembering much of his past - including his enmity to the PCs. He even claims not to remember his guild affiliation!<br /> <br /> He's obviously playing the PCs. Right?<br /> <br /> Could a Deceived mummy be rehabilitated?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .) The &quot;Word of Lethe&quot; is an apocryphal Utterance of particular notoriety; it is rumored to hold the power over the Sekhem of other mummies. Its Tier 3 effect is, as per the legends, strong enough to force an Arisen (or a Shuankhsen) back to the sleep of death in an instant, at the cost of a piece of the user's own Sekhem.<br /> <br /> If such an Utterance really exists, which most Deathless refuse to believe, it is likely that only the secret, forbidden ren-hekau name magic of the Deceived will protect a mummy against the Word of Lethe.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:30:26-07:00","id":89132,"title":"","content":"In the days of the Nameless Empire, they were the one Guild to speak out against the Shan'iatu and the Rite of Return. It seems that their entire Guild was sacrificed by the sorcerer-kings or was, at the very least, hunted to the brink of extinction by the other five Guilds. I suspect, while they may know more than the typical Arisen, that they do have Memory as the Arisen do, only because I imagine the Shuankhsen being in a unique circumstance.<br /> <br /> CAS has said that there is a wider gap between the Arisen and the Deceived than, say, Kindred and Belial's Brood in <i>Vampire: the Requiem</i>, but that they are still Deathless. That implies that they are 'true' Mummies, unlike the Shuankhsen, sadikh, or fasad who are all considered Lifeless.<br /> <br /> I also suspect that their knowledge of true name magic is very dangerous. While the Deceived seem to have some connection to Apotheosis, I think that end game state of being will be of some protection from the Deceived, because one of Apotheosis's benefits is that the Mummy 'reclaims their true name, effectively becoming invisible to the supernatural world,'<br /> <br /> I intend on using the Deceived in my own game, but at this point I'm just using the time before their supplement's release to build up the rumors of their existence. They shouldn't show up right away if it's your players' first Mummy game. Their existence is blasphemous, and the reveal of their machinations should be long in coming. So until <i>Book of the Deceived </i>is released, I'm using this time to plant those Chekov's guns <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:01:56-07:00","id":89145,"title":"","content":"I recall reading something in Guildhalls of the Deathless which said that mortal sorcerers are interesting because they seem to be using the same kind of Nomenclature magic that the Lost Guild were meant to have practiced. Actually, Guildhalls brought up mortal sorcerers quite frequently, and given the apparent connection I'm rather hoping to see something on them in the Book of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Anyway, at present, I've not really got any particular plans to include them in my games. If I were to use them, I'd probably have them work like high-Memory Mummies, probably post-Apotheosis, that use the Sesha-Hebsu Utterances (and other Utterances along the same lines) from Guildhalls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:29:55-07:00","id":89609,"title":"","content":"thanks for information and ideas... I think I will use Deceived as main antagonist, but as a hidden one - before the Book of Deceived will be released ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2492-wenoush","name":"wenoush","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}